From: Octavo (local foliate-js patch set)
Subject: [PATCH 0001] paginator: keep the position on blank pages

On a page with no visible node (a blank column left by forced breaks, a
block spanning whole columns, a 100vh title), getVisibleRange() fell back
to the section's <body>. The relocate CFI then named only the section, and
the paginator's anchor did too, so any re-layout (resize, fold, font load,
setStyles) or a restore of the saved CFI jumped to the section's first page.

- Location: report a collapsed range at the first node after the page
  (where reading resumes), or the end of the last element.
- Anchor: anchor a blank page to its page fraction, the inverse of what
  #scrollToAnchor() does with a number.

Pages with any visible node take the same path as before; CFIs on 1,546 of
1,546 non-blank pages were byte-identical with and without the patch.
Vetted in docs/notes/foliate-blank-page-upstream.md (branch
claude/foliate-blank-page-vetting-1aa980, e1946c0). Not sent upstream.

Apply from the repo root:
  git apply --directory=ReaderWeb/foliate-js ReaderWeb/foliate-js/patches/0001-blank-page-position.patch
